From 081af71388b3ab9d28a8615ffb5933afcfaec47a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "exe.dev user" <exedev@erbium-qemu.exe.xyz>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:20:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] erbium: model CPU warm-reset hold and host-controlled startup

Wire SoftReset warm hold to execution gating and defer CPU-originated resets to safe cycle boundaries. Resample MINION_BOOT and hart reset state at release without reapplying CLI configuration or touching memory/peripherals. Keep CPU cold pulses and whole-system POR distinct.

Add --start-held as an explicit startup/POR profile, including no-ELF socket service. Exercise held masks, changed boot PC, repeated socket uploads, preserved MRAM/SRAM and mailboxes, CPU CSR reset, WFI/reconnection, CPU-originated hold, cold pulses, xSPI-only reset, and default running launches with a standalone stdlib Python test.

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
